Feature: EN 1999 structural scene
  The aluminium snapshot and its check report project to a deterministic, locale-free 3D scene, a set of 2D diagrams and drag handles.

  Further specification assertions, asserted by the Rust unit tests of the crate and not by the platform adapters:
  - extrusions show their section and the heat-affected zones of the welds: Given the compliant aluminium roof purlin When the scene is projected Then entity "purlin-1" is a member of 6.00 m whose section outline area equals 2·b·t_f + (h − 2·t_f)·t_w And entity "purlin-1" carries 5 translucent HAZ bands whose rectangles are the strips reduced by ρ_o,haz
  - class 4 plates show the effective section: Given the non-compliant thin-walled beam and its check report When the scene is projected Then entity "beam-fail:effective" is a ghost of the section with the plates thinned by ρ_c And the member has error style, a diagonal hatch, a failure glyph and a buckling mode shape
  - connections show plate, bolt grid, fillet weld and HAZ extent: Given the compliant aluminium roof purlin When the scene is projected Then entity "support-weld:bolts" is a 2 by 2 grid with the pitch and gauge of connection "support-weld" And entity "support-weld:haz" is as long as the HAZ width of the weld
  - handles keep the plate elements tied to the section: Given the compliant aluminium roof purlin When the depth handle of "purlin-1" is dragged to 0.160 m Then one write sets "sections[id=sec-i120].height" to 0.160 m And one write sets the web plate width to 0.140 m
  - diagrams agree with the closed forms: Given the compliant aluminium roof purlin and its check report When the diagrams are built Then the buckling marker of "purlin-1" lies on the curve of its buckling class And an independent Python oracle reproduces the section areas, the buckling classes A and B, the ρ_c reduction, the HAZ widths, the S–N law, the fire temperatures and the shell reduction
  - members carry stations and kernel-computed modes: Given the compliant roof purlin and the multi-failure fixture When the scene is projected Then members are coloured per check station with the largest station equal to the governing member utilisation And the flexural mode has the Euler load of the declared support, the lateral-torsional moment rises with shorter unrestrained length, and the deflection line peaks at the computed deflection
  - the mode track scrubs flexural and lateral-torsional eigenforms one layer at a time: Given a document whose members have a flexural and a lateral-torsional buckling check When the scene is projected Then a "mode" track of kind Mode snaps over indices 1 to 2 only when two mode layers exist And every keyframe reveals one mode layer whose entities carry a harmonic mode overlay of that index
  - every check outcome tones its owner in 3D: Given the full EN 1999 showcase with its filed and unfiled check report When the scene is projected Then every check routes to a drawn row, to a section or alloy no row uses, or to the document badge And a sheet, a shell and a fire scenario are coloured by the worst check routed to them And the row that is selected for a check is the row that owns it
  - every numeric field has a viewport grip: Given the full EN 1999 showcase and the numeric fields of the snapshot schema When the handles of every entity are built Then each numeric field is written by a geometric grip or by a gauge grip with the schema step and a typed edit kind And the gauge of "bucklingLengthT" writes the current value at zero drag and twenty steps per metre
  - the torsional and welded-member buckling curves carry the design point: Given a member with a torsional buckling check When the diagrams are built Then "torsional:purlin-1" holds χ_T over λ̄_T with the design point of the check And "torsional-length:purlin-1" holds N_b,T,Rd over L_cr,T with the demand line and a marker that drags the torsional buckling length And "haz-buckling:<member>" holds χ, κ and κ·χ with κ·χ equal to the product, and an independent Python recomputation reproduces the three diagrams
  - the heat-affected zone of a weld run names its strength factors: Given a weld run on a member of alloy 6082 When the scene is projected Then the HAZ zone of the run states b_haz, ρ_o,haz and ρ_u,haz of the alloy at the plate thickness in English and German
  - checks without a dedicated diagram are outcome bars: Given the full EN 1999 showcase When the diagrams are built Then every applicable check outside the drawn families is a bar of the outcome diagram of its owning row against the limit line at 1 And no drawn family appears among the bars
